@startuml
' ============================================================================
' METADATA
'   author:       TheRobotDrafts Examples
' '   description:  Order fulfillment with parallel pack/ship, three swimlanes, and object flow.
'   usecase:      Teach fork/join bars, swimlane partitions, object nodes, control flow.
'   complexity:   medium
'   domain:       logistics
' ============================================================================
title Example Activity - Medium Order Fulfillment

' SWIMLANES (partitions) group actions by who performs them.
' Declare a lane with |LaneName|; subsequent actions belong to it
' until another |LaneName| header switches the current partition.
' Rendered as vertical columns separated by dashed lines.

|Customer|
start

' Actions can produce OBJECT NODES — data tokens that travel along
' OBJECT FLOW edges (as opposed to pure control flow).
:Submit order request;
note right
  <<object node>>
  OrderRequest
  (data token passed downstream)
end note

|Billing|
:Validate payment method;

if (Card authorized?) then (yes)
  :Capture payment;
else (no)
  |Customer|
  :Update payment details;
  stop
endif

' A FORK NODE splits one control flow into multiple CONCURRENT flows.
' It renders as a thick synchronization bar (horizontal/vertical line).
fork
  |Billing|
  :Issue invoice;
  :Send receipt email;
fork again
  |Warehouse|
  :Reserve inventory;
  :Pick items from shelf;
end fork
' A JOIN NODE ("end fork") WAITS for ALL concurrent flows to arrive
' before a single flow proceeds. Fork and join are synchronization points.

|Warehouse|
:Pack shipment;

:Generate shipping label;

:Dispatch with courier;

|Customer|
:Receive package;
stop

' TEACHING NOTES:
'   - Fork/join model true concurrency (parallel execution).
'   - A decision (if) chooses ONE branch; a fork runs ALL branches.
'   - Object flow carries data; control flow carries only a token of control.
'   - Swimlanes are a presentation choice — they do not change semantics.
@enduml
